cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use HSLM ternary neural network findings, please cite this work. HSLM achieves 20× memory compression with PPL 125.3 on TinyStories."
title: "Trinity B001: Ternary Neural Networks — HSLM-1.95M Scientific Framework"
abstract: "We present HSLM-1.95M, a 1.95M parameter ternary language model using balanced ternary weights {-1, 0, +1} achieving 1.58 bits/trit (20× memory compression vs FP32). Key innovations include: (1) Sacred Attention with φ-based scaling (scale = d_k^(-φ^-3) ≈ 0.236); (2) T-JEPA (Ternary JEPA) with consciousness gate for masked prediction; (3) Cosine learning rate with φ-warmup; (4) Ternary SGD with convergence proof; (5) TF3 packing (8 weights in 16 bits). Results: PPL 125.3 ± 2.1 on TinyStories, 385 KB model size, 1200 tokens/sec inference. Pure Zig 0.15.x implementation with zero external dependencies. Complete reproducibility artifacts including Docker environment, MLSys reproducibility card, and algorithm pseudocode."
